I am trying to execute R-script via Renjin. The script has tests to test auto corellation , hence uses orcutt method.

So, the few lines of script will be:

      library(orcutt)
      y <- lm( sales ~ oos + trend + lagsales ,data= DataPrep)

      x <- cochrane.orcutt(y)
      b <-x$coefficients[2]

      a <- x$rho

      CoefCochIncpt    <- x$Cochrane.Orcutt$coefficients[1]
      CoefCochoos      <- x$Cochrane.Orcutt$coefficients[2]
      CoefCochtrend    <- x$Cochrane.Orcutt$coefficients[3]
      CoefCochlagsales <- x$Cochrane.Orcutt$coefficients[4]
      CoefCochIncpt
      CoefCochoos
      CoefCochtrend
      CoefCochlagsales

On executing the script it gives the following error:

org.renjin.eval.EvalException: orcutt could not be found

